oney at stake but the risk is off  the charts part of the critique of the  defy ecosystem and many of the smart  contract platforms by the bitcoin  community is that ultimately there is  too much flippant attitude towards how  much risk is actually being taken not  only by the protocol developers but also  by the users if you are going to have  hundreds of millions of dollars or  billions of dollars at stake  you better damn be sure that you have  high security and that you are resistant  to these types of attacks ultimately  what we're watching play out here is  simply a market being developed the  nefarious actors are going to continue  to exploit these types of issues until  it becomes standard practice and  well-accepted structure on how to  prevent them nobody wants to see 182  million dollars stolen but ultimately  this is a lesson learned for every  single protocol developer every single  d5 application make sure that people  can't just go get a flash loan take over  your governance process and then  withdraw the funds to their own wallet  that sounded insane until we literally  watched it happen yesterday hopefully  the entire ecosystem and industry will  be better off for this having happened  because we'll learn a valuable lesson  maybe the funds will get recovered maybe  they won't but 182 million dollars is  better than if someone had went and  stolen billions and billions once we got  later down the road hey you did you like  this video great we make five of them a  day and post them here on this channel  make sure you subscribe like the video  and see you next time
 

